# Design System Rules

The application must have one coherent visual language.

Do not invent new visual styles for individual pages.

## Brand direction

The skincare storefront should feel:

- premium
- warm
- elegant
- modern
- trustworthy
- editorial
- minimal

The admin application should feel:

- professional
- sophisticated
- operational
- clean
- data-focused

Avoid:

- generic SaaS purple gradients
- neon colors
- excessive glassmorphism
- excessive shadows
- childish rounded interfaces
- inconsistent border radii
- random colors
- unnecessary animations

## Tokens

Use centralized design tokens for:

- colors
- typography
- spacing
- radius
- shadows
- borders
- transitions

Do not hardcode arbitrary colors throughout components.

Use the existing Tailwind/theme tokens.

If a new token is required, add it centrally rather than introducing one-off values.

## Typography

Use the established typography hierarchy.

Do not introduce random font sizes.

Maintain consistent:

- display
- h1
- h2
- h3
- body
- small
- label
- caption

## Spacing

Use the established spacing scale.

Avoid arbitrary margins such as:

mt-[37px]

unless there is a strong design reason.

Prefer the project's spacing tokens.

## Buttons

Use the shared button component.

Do not create custom button styles inside individual pages unless a genuinely new variant is required.

Buttons must have:

- default
- hover
- active
- disabled
- loading
states where applicable.

## Forms

Use consistent:

- labels
- inputs
- validation messages
- helper text
- focus states

## Cards

Cards should use consistent:

- border
- radius
- padding
- background
- hover behavior

Do not create a different card style for every dashboard section.

## Tables

Use a shared table pattern.

Tables must support:

- loading
- empty
- error
- pagination where appropriate
- responsive behavior

## Status badges

Use semantic status styles.

Examples:

SUCCESS
WARNING
ERROR
INFO
NEUTRAL

Do not invent random colors for individual statuses.

## Icons

Use one icon library consistently.

Do not mix multiple unrelated icon libraries.

Icons should support the content rather than dominate it.

## Animation

Use subtle transitions.

Avoid unnecessary animation.

Respect reduced-motion preferences.

## Design preservation

When implementing functionality into Lovable-generated UI:

DO NOT redesign the interface unless explicitly instructed.

Preserve the established:

- colors
- typography
- spacing
- component appearance
- layout
- responsive behavior

The existing UI is the visual source of truth.